Write a SystemVerilog function that:

🔹 Requirements
Takes an array of integers as input
Returns:
1 → if the array has more even numbers
-1 → if the array has more odd numbers
0 → if both are equal
🔹 Testbench Task
Create an array with random values (size 10)
Call the function
Display:
Array values
Count of even & odd numbers
Final result
💡 Example

Input Array:
{2, 5, 8, 7, 6}

Even count: 3
Odd count: 2

Output: 1 (more evens)

🎯 Bonus Challenge
Modify the function to return both counts using output arguments
Or make it generic (works with dynamic arrays)


// start

module compare_module;
int a[10];

function int compare(input int a[10]);
int even = 0 ;
int odd = 0 ;
for (int i =0;i<10;i++) begin
if(a[i]%2==0) 
even++;
else
odd++;  
end
if (even > odd)
return 1;
else if (even < odd)
return -1;
else
return 0;
endfunction         

initial begin
int count;
  
foreach (a[i]) begin
  a[i] = $urandom_range(0,100);
$display("a[%0d] = %0d", i, a[i]);
end

count = compare(a);
if (count == 1) begin

$display("Output: 1 (more evens)");
end
else if (count == -1) begin
              
$display("Output: -1 (more odds)");
end
else begin

$display("Output: 0 (equal evens and odds)");
end
end
endmodule

